def render_executive(review):
    return f'''<section class="hero"><div class="hero-content"><div class="eyebrow">Executive summary · submission instructions</div><h1>Validate automatically.<br>Select a slot separately.</h1><p class="lead">There is currently no approved new submission TIFF. Do not select a file from this page at present. Do not upload an archived reference just because it opens correctly or contains only values in [0,1].</p></div></section>
<section class="section"><h2>The exact path to an eligible submission</h2><ol class="submission-steps">
<li><strong>Pass preflight before a scientific run.</strong> Configure the explicitly assigned lane, complete external registry and a frozen comparable holdout baseline. <code>python scripts/check_run_preflight.py</code> currently exits 1 with the real blockers. The existing data/cache and pinned shared tools now pass their local integrity checks.</li>
<li><strong>Use the shared evaluation path.</strong> Load the existing feature cache and read-only pinned shared evaluator/writer. Withhold whole fault segments/components with a buffer; construct catalogue features from visible faults only; mask those faults pixel-exactly. Never score a final full-catalogue TIFF as if it were an independent out-of-fold model.</li>
<li><strong>Run scientific gates in order.</strong> Test every feature alone, both polarities and each fold, before trusting it. Treat AUC above 0.90 as leakage until resolved. Check the surface against every registry member <em>before</em> placing dots. Stop and log a duplicate if correlation exceeds 0.90. On final dots also stop if more than 70% are within 3 pixels of any one member.</li>
<li><strong>Beat a frozen same-protocol baseline.</strong> Report pooled HOLDOUT-DTI with evaluator version, withheld-positive count and a 95% spatial-cluster interval. Require a positive paired improvement interval, not a mean-only improvement. The metric uses alpha 0.2, beta 0.8 and the 300 m triangular kernel. A projection is never a score.</li>
<li><strong>Serialize and independently re-read.</strong> The writer must produce one float32 GeoTIFF band on the exact sample CRS, shape and transform. Verify no NaN inside the footprint, values in [0,1], footprint handling, file SHA-256 and no catalogue overlap. A zero-outside variant has no NaN anywhere; that is a numeric-range property, not a guarantee of portal acceptance.</li>
<li><strong>Publish an eligible candidate, not a slot decision.</strong> Give it a content-bound unique name and a note of at most 140 characters. <code>python scripts/check_promotion.py CARD.json</code> checks the evidence schema, but does not authenticate its measurements, authorize an upload or inspect a TIFF by itself.</li>
<li><strong>Only the separate selector may use a real slot.</strong> It must check the actual current submission-page cap and remaining allowance. This review makes no selection. Account-side upload requires access that is not available here; no DrivenData automation occurs.</li>
<li><strong>At the competition form, only after all prior steps pass:</strong> choose the approved single-band <code>.tif</code> (or ZIP containing exactly that TIFF), paste its published ≤140-character note, and submit. Preserve the organizer's receipt bound to the exact filename/hash before labeling a result ORGANIZER-CONFIRMED. There is no approved file or portal note to copy today.</li>
</ol></section>
<section class="section"><h2>Current decision, with no human-inspection loophole</h2><ul>{''.join('<li>' + esc(x) + '</li>' for x in review['blockers'])}</ul><p><strong>Verdict: negative.</strong> No new TIFF, no new HOLDOUT-DTI, no slot used. This is an honest negative deliverable, not a completed unique-submission generation run.</p><p><a href="data/run_card_2026-10-25.json" download>Download current JSON run card</a> · {source('evidence/current_submission_audit.json','Automated archive audit')} · <a href="archive.html">Historical files — DO NOT SUBMIT</a></p></section>
<section class="section"><h2>About the previous range error</h2><p>The text “Predicted values must be in range [0, 1]” alone does not establish whether NaN, a negative value, a sentinel, an out-of-range probability or a masked-read interpretation caused the rejection. The hardened existing local writer rejects invalid interior probabilities rather than silently clipping them. The upstream read-only writer has a separate sanitization contract; it was not used to emit a candidate in this review. The independent validator re-reads disk bytes, including nodata semantics. Fixing the range is necessary; it cannot establish uniqueness or performance.</p><p>{source('evidence/range_validator_forensics_2026-10-03.json','Historical exact-file range forensics')}</p></section>
<section class="section"><h2>Official review links</h2><ul><li><a href="https://www.drivendata.org/competitions/306/competition-doe-gems/page/967/">Problem, metric and submission format</a></li><li><a href="https://www.drivendata.org/competitions/306/competition-doe-gems/leaderboard/">Competition leaderboard</a> — not freshly read here</li><li><a href="https://docs.nlr.gov/docs/fy26osti/96647.pdf">Rules PDF supplied in the brief</a> — not freshly retrieved here</li><li><a href="https://github.com/drivendataorg/gems-prize-reference-solution">Official reference solution</a> — pinned GitHub source inspected in this review</li></ul></section>'''


def render_hypotheses(review):
    cards = []
    for h in review["hypotheses"]:
        cards.append(f'''<article class="card span-6"><div class="rank">Rank {h['rank']} · {esc(h['id'])}</div><h3>{esc(h['name'])}</h3>
<p><strong>Layers:</strong> {esc(h['layers'])}</p><p><strong>Physical signature:</strong> {esc(h['signature'])}</p><p><strong>Why an omitted fault:</strong> {esc(h['missing_fault_rationale'])}</p><p><strong>Difference from local code:</strong> {esc(h['difference_from_repo'])}</p><p><strong>Non-fault mimic:</strong> {esc(h['non_fault_mimic'])}</p><p><strong>Expected benefit:</strong> {esc(h['expected_dti_improvement'])}</p><p><strong>Cost:</strong> {esc(h['implementation_cost'])}</p><p><strong>Availability:</strong> {esc(h['availability'])}</p><p class="small">{esc(h['status'])} <a href="{esc(h['source'])}">Official source review link</a> (not freshly retrieved here).</p></article>''')
    return f'''<section class="section"><div class="eyebrow">Current hypothesis slate · no experiments run</div><h1>New information,<br>not a new filename.</h1><p class="lead">These are geological conjectures, not verified discoveries or score forecasts. Ranking is qualitative. The top proposal is not an assigned parallel-run lane and must not be implemented until preflight is resolved.</p><p>Only the pre-existing cache and hash-pinned mirror bytes are verified available. No official-source metadata or license has been newly authenticated by a mirror hash. No high-resolution external-data idea is marked viable without its required coverage/bytes.</p><div class="grid">{''.join(cards)}</div></section>'''


def render_review(review, audit, priority, official):
    concurrent = review.get("concurrent_claim_review", {})
    concurrent_panel = ""
    if concurrent:
        concurrent_panel = f'''<section class="section"><h2>Concurrent H38-1 claim: rejected</h2><p>{esc(concurrent['summary'])}</p><p>{source(concurrent['path'], 'Byte-history and pinned novelty proof')} · Original claimed card and check are preserved as historical evidence, not approval.</p></section>'''
    rows = []
    for repo in priority["repositories"]:
        for raster in repo["priority_rasters"]:
            rows.append(f'''<tr><td>{esc(repo['repository'].split('/')[-1])}<br><code>{esc(repo['commit'][:12])}</code></td><td><a href="{esc(raster['source'])}">{esc(raster['path'].split('/')[-1])}</a></td><td>{raster['nonzero_inside_px']:,}</td><td>{'PASS' if raster['hard_checks_passed'] else 'FAIL: ' + esc(', '.join(raster['hard_failures']))}</td><td><code>{esc(raster['sha256'])}</code></td></tr>''')
    overlap = []
    for row in audit["final_dots"]["rows"]:
        overlap.append(f'''<tr><td>{esc(row['registry_id'])}</td><td>{row['raw_spearman']:.6f}</td><td>{row['candidate_dot_overlap_within_3px']:.2%}</td><td>{'DUPLICATE' if row['duplicate'] else 'No violation measured'}</td></tr>''')
    f = audit["forensic"]
    return f'''<section class="hero"><div class="hero-content"><div class="eyebrow">Current automated review · 2026-10-25</div><h1>Prove the bytes.<br>Bound the claims.</h1><p class="lead">No new candidate was generated. This page reports a read-only audit of previous submissions, source integrity and shared-tool software tests. It does not backdate a surface check or manufacture a geological holdout result.</p></div></section>{concurrent_panel}
<section class="section"><h2>What is directly verified</h2><ul><li>The GEMSDOE32 champion contains {f['champion_pixels']:,} positive footprint pixels. It equals the solo baseline after removing exactly {f['removed_solo_to_champion']:,} catalogue-near pixels, with {f['added_solo_to_champion']} additions.</li><li>GEMSDOE36 contains every champion dot plus {f['g36_additional_pixels']:,} others. Its name does not establish an independent method.</li><li>GEMSDOE25 and GEMSDOE30 have identical footprint predictions. GEMSDOE28 solo and GEMSDOE31 solo do too. Byte hashes may differ because packaging and outside-footprint conventions differ.</li><li>The archived primary passes two format validators but fails the final-dot uniqueness threshold. Its original pre-placement surface is unavailable; no substitute surface was invented.</li></ul><p>{source('evidence/current_submission_audit.json','Full computed evidence')} · {source('registry/protocol_assets.json','Read-only shared-source pins')}</p></section>
<section class="section"><h2>Why thinning and pruning can help</h2><p>For fixed truth size G, the stipulated Tversky expression can be written <code>S = TP / (0.2·TP + 0.2·FP + 0.8·G)</code>. An addition improves it only when its marginal <code>ΔTP/ΔFP &gt; 0.2·S/(1−0.2·S)</code>. Deleting low-efficiency predictions reverses that tradeoff. Sparse dots may preserve triangular-kernel coverage while reducing redundant prediction mass.</p><p>This algebra is not a new score. The missing organizer truth prevents measuring the champion's actual TP/FP changes. Its reported advantage is plausibly emission hygiene; no causal score explanation or geothermal discovery is established. No candidate in this review is shown to exceed the user-supplied result.</p></section>
<section class="section"><h2>Nine-site artifact audit</h2><p>Pinned Git-tree blob identities and SHA-256 values identify the inspected bytes. These are owner repositories, not organizer receipts. The variants are educational references only. Three GEMSDOE31 “allfinite” variants failed the local outside/nodata convention checks; this is not proof of a portal rejection.</p><div class="table-wrap"><table><thead><tr><th>Repository / pinned commit</th><th>Artifact (source)</th><th>Positive cells</th><th>Local format</th><th>File SHA-256</th></tr></thead><tbody>{''.join(rows)}</tbody></table></div><p>{source('evidence/priority_repository_audit.json','Complete priority audit JSON')}</p></section>
<section class="section"><h2>Historical primary: final-dot comparison</h2><p>Directional overlap counts <em>all</em> primary dots at distance ≤3 pixels from each reference, not a dot sample. Raw Spearman covers every footprint pixel; the shared comparator also records a separately labeled kernel sample in JSON. No statistical number in this table is a DTI score.</p><div class="table-wrap"><table><thead><tr><th>Reference</th><th>Exact raw Spearman</th><th>Primary dots within 3 px</th><th>Result</th></tr></thead><tbody>{''.join(overlap)}</tbody></table></div><p><strong>Scope:</strong> priority artifacts plus local archive, not the absent complete external parallel-run registry. One measured duplicate is already sufficient to reject this archived primary as a new lane.</p></section>
<section class="section"><h2>Official evidence and limits</h2><p>The official reference was inspected at commit <code>{esc(official['commit'])}</code>. It describes fault detection and supports CPU-only training environments. Its training loss uses alpha 0.2 and beta 0.8; it does not provide a submission receipt or authenticate this repository's mirrored training files.</p><p><a href="{esc(official['source'])}">Pinned official notebook</a> · {source('evidence/official_reference_audit.json','Source/cell audit')} · {source('evidence/shared_template_contract.json','Synthetic shared-tool contract tests')}</p><p>Official non-GitHub hosts are outside this runtime's allowed outbound hosts. Current leaderboard maxima, deadlines, external-data licenses and the current weekly cap were not freshly authenticated. Older source-feed observations are retained with their actual dates, never relabeled as new retrievals.</p></section>
<section class="section"><h2>What happens next</h2><p>Resolve the method assignment, complete shared registry and a comparable frozen baseline. Run only that lane, within three experiments or two hours. Use canaries → surface duplicate stop → pooled paired holdout → final-dot duplicate stop → shared writer → independent byte validation → promotion eligibility. A separate selector decides any real slot.</p><p>{source('knowledge/51_current_review_and_next_steps.md','Detailed audit, three-pass record and next steps')} · <a href="executive-summary.html">Exact submission instructions</a> · <a href="archive.html">Research TIFF archive (not approved)</a></p></section>'''
